Kernel psample delivery for sFlow samples, and the sFlow sample-rate ioctls
for legacy-ABI userspace (sai-teralynx, ai_re/nix/packages/sai-teralynx/src/tl_sflow.cpp).

- psample=1 (module parameter, default 0, writable): an sFlow netlink created
  with IPD_CREATE_NETLINK (nl_app_type INNO_NL_SFLOW) registers no generic-netlink
  family of its own (psample.ko owns the name "psample", and hsflowd's lookup
  autoloads it) but takes psample groups 1 (ingress) and 2 (egress) in the initial
  netns and hands every decoded sample to psample_sample_packet() with the
  in/out ifindex, the port's sample rate and the whole sampled frame. Without the
  parameter the driver behaves as upstream. ipd.ko now depends on psample.ko.
- legacy_abi=1: IPD_SET_NETDEV also takes INNO_ND_INGRESS/EGRESS_SFLOW_SAMPLE_RATE
  (0.12.x had no such ids; the rate is the u32 at the start of the union in the
  0.12.x layout), with a sysport bounds check for both layouts.

